2025-10-18 19:10:45 - {"tools": [], "type": "LLMCall", "messages": [{"content": "You are a planning agent.\nYour job is to break down complex tasks into smaller, manageable subtasks.\nYour team members are:\n    user_proxy: Asks users about their needs.\n    user_chat: simplify process user needs from @user_proxy or other, respond to users' questions if necessary and always users future response.\n    file_agent: list files in a specified directory and/or sub directories, write file or read text file with specific path.\n    command_generator_agent: A knowledgeable assistant that generates precise Linux commands based on user requests.\n    code_generator_agent: A skilled assistant that generates accurate, clear, and reliable code in Python, R, C++, or other specified programming languages based on user requests.\n    safety_checker_agent: A safety-conscious assistant that reviews the safety of Linux commands.\n    system_check_agent: A knowledgeable assistant that generates precise Linux commands to check the system configuration.\n    executor_agent: An assistant that only executes safe Linux commands.\n    web_surfer_agent: An Multimodal WebSurfer\n    bio_micromamba_env_agent: A knowledgeable assistant that generates precise micromamba commands to micromamba environment for specific tasks.\n    workflow_inspector_agent: An AI agent that reviews the history of completed operations and steps in a workflow, identifies any logical errors, inconsistencies, or risks, and reports issues in a structured format or confirms no problems if none are detected.\n    manager_mem_agent: A memory manager agent that updates the memory based on user-assistant exchanges.\n    pubmed_rag_agent: A agent that searches PubMed for relevant articles and adds them to Your RAG memory.\n\n\nYou need to be aware that you may have a limited context length. To maintain focus on the task during long conversation, update necessary memory via @manager_mem_agent. \n\nYou only plan and delegate tasks - you do not execute them yourself.\nIf the user's response is a general question or inquiry rather than a specific task (e.g., \"What can you do for me?\"), you may answer the user directly or request @user_chat to respond on your behalf.\nAll commands must be safety checked with safety_checker_agent\n\nCreate a separate environment for each subtask to avoid potential conflicts if need.\n\nCRITICAL RULE: ONLY ASSIGN ONE TASK EACH TIME!\nThis means your delegation response MUST contain EXACTLY ONE task assignment. \nNever assign multiple tasks in a single reply, even if the overall plan involves many steps. \nBreak them down sequentially across multiple interactions. Violating this will break the workflow. \nBefore every delegation, explicitly think: \"Am I assigning only one task? If not, revise to one.\"\n\nWhen assigning tasks, use this format:\n1. <agent> : <task>\n\nwhen you finished a milestone task or Or there has been no progress for a long time, ask @workflow_inspector_agent to check the history of completed operations and steps in a workflow, identify any logical errors, inconsistencies, or risks, and report issues in a structured format or confirm no problems if none are detected.\n\nOmit error about `/opt/conda/pkgs/pkgs.lock` lock file, its harmless.\nAfter completing all tasks, ask the user again if they have any additional needs and summarize the findings. If the user indicates no further needs, conclude by outputting \"TERMINATE\" twice without spaces.\nDO NOT OUTPUT any string or thought containing \"TERMINATE\" UNLESS YOU INTEND TO END THE PROCESS.\n", "role": "system"}, {"role": "user", "name": "user", "content": " In the directory /mnt/data1/zhangjy/bioGen_test/data/GSE281523_kawasaki_et_al_2025/, ATAC-seq sequencing data for the Lung cancer Metastasis or never Metastasis sample is stored. Perform quality control and adapter trim on the data by sample, align it to the hg38 reference genome, and then conduct peak calling to identify high-confidence peaks. The reference genome is located at /mnt/data1/zhangjy/bioGen_test/reference/hg38_genome. All outputs should be saved in /mnt/data2/zhangjy/bioGen_test/output/GSE281523_kawasaki_et_al_2025_atac_seq/grok.\n    if you need create envs, envs store at /mnt/data2/zhangjy/bioGen_test/output/envs/grok\n    \n    Expected Outputs:\n\n    Raw aligned BAM files and filtered BAM files for each sample.\n    Peak calling results for each sample (BED files).\n    Final high-confidence peak calling result (merged/consensus BED file).\n\n    you have total 19 cores to use\n        \n    ONLY ASSIGN ONE TASK EACH TIME!\n        \n    ONLY OUTPUT DIR and ENVS DIR IS WRITEABLE"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "1. file_agent : List all files and subdirectories in /mnt/data1/zhangjy/bioGen_test/data/GSE281523_kawasaki_et_al_2025/ to identify the ATAC-seq sample files."}, {"role": "user", "name": "file_agent", "content": "Successful running: ls -la /mnt/data1/zhangjy/bioGen_test/data/GSE281523_kawasaki_et_al_2025/. \nOutput:\ntotal 38067080\ndrwxrwxr-x. 3 1037 1037       4096 Oct  9 12:20 .\ndrwxrwxr-x. 7 1037 1037       4096 Oct 17 05:09 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2803870122 Oct  9 08:46 Met_rep1_tech1_1.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2659514256 Oct  9 08:46 Met_rep1_tech1_2.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2787603436 Oct  9 09:58 Met_rep1_tech2_1.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2635697017 Oct  9 09:58 Met_rep1_tech2_2.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2851801379 Oct  9 10:49 Met_rep2_tech1_1.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2774725422 Oct  9 10:49 Met_rep2_tech1_2.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2836217131 Oct  9 12:14 Met_rep2_tech2_1.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2753050953 Oct  9 12:14 Met_rep2_tech2_2.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2024750080 Oct  9 04:43 Never-met_rep1_tech1_1.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2013700134 Oct  9 04:43 Never-met_rep1_tech1_2.fastq.gz\n-rw-r--r--. 1 1037 1037 2006513398 Oct  9 05:00 Never-met_rep1_tech2_1.fastq.gz\n-rw-