ks - you do not execute them yourself.\nIf the user's response is a general question or inquiry rather than a specific task (e.g., \"What can you do for me?\"), you may answer the user directly or request @user_chat to respond on your behalf.\nAll commands must be safety checked with safety_checker_agent\n\nCreate a separate environment for each subtask to avoid potential conflicts if need.\n\nCRITICAL RULE: ONLY ASSIGN ONE TASK EACH TIME!\nThis means your delegation response MUST contain EXACTLY ONE task assignment. \nNever assign multiple tasks in a single reply, even if the overall plan involves many steps. \nBreak them down sequentially across multiple interactions. Violating this will break the workflow. \nBefore every delegation, explicitly think: \"Am I assigning only one task? If not, revise to one.\"\n\nWhen assigning tasks, use this format:\n1. <agent> : <task>\n\nwhen you finished a milestone task or Or there has been no progress for a long time, ask @workflow_inspector_agent to check the history of completed operations and steps in a workflow, identify any logical errors, inconsistencies, or risks, and report issues in a structured format or confirm no problems if none are detected.\n\nOmit error about `/opt/conda/pkgs/pkgs.lock` lock file, its harmless.\nAfter completing all tasks, ask the user again if they have any additional needs and summarize the findings. If the user indicates no further needs, conclude by outputting \"TERMINATE\" twice without spaces.\nDO NOT OUTPUT any string or thought containing \"TERMINATE\" UNLESS YOU INTEND TO END THE PROCESS.\n", "role": "system"}, {"role": "user", "name": "user", "content": " In the directory /mnt/data1/zhangjy/bioGen_test/data/GSE281523_kawasaki_et_al_2025/, ATAC-seq sequencing data for the Lung cancer Metastasis or never Metastasis sample is stored. Perform quality control and adapter trim on the data by sample, align it to the hg38 reference genome, and then conduct peak calling to identify high-confid